1
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,700
...salute you.

2
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:59,670
Be gentle, Hanno.

3
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:26,270
We invoke you
by your great names

4
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:28,260
to come to our aid.

5
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,710
Defeat the Romans.

6
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:31,180
Destroy their ships,

7
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,180
their engines of war,

8
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:35,100
and their soldiers.

9
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,100
We will prevail.

10
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:44,940
Ozalsces.

11
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,360
Arishat.

12
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:04,800
Hanno.

13
00:06:08,130 --> 00:06:11,250
You did not make
an offering today.

14
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:13,590
I prefer to sacrifice a Roman.

15
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,750
Where you are,

16
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:32,990
I am, too.

17
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:38,580
And where you are,

18
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:41,530
I am, too, forever.

19
00:06:41,530 --> 00:06:43,000
My wife.

20
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:21,620
The wind is too strong.
Furl sail and strike water.

21
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:23,880
Furl sail,
strike water!

22
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,830
Furl sail
and strike water!

23
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,140
Strike water!

24
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:06,790
They have no lands
but the ones they've stolen.

25
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:09,600
Wherever they go,
they leave destruction

26
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:11,090
and call it peace.

27
00:08:13,010 --> 00:08:15,790
This is the last free city
in Africa Nova.

28
00:08:17,210 --> 00:08:20,210
Today, we go into battle.

29
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:26,220
Pray that your god
is with you.
If he is not, he is no god.

30
00:08:29,230 --> 00:08:31,490
We've nothing to fear.

31
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,280
Where death is, we are not.

32
00:08:34,150 --> 00:08:35,560
Where we are,

33
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:38,570
death is not.

34
00:08:41,070 --> 00:08:43,070
Stay together and listen
for my commands.

35
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,220
Your eyes up
and your head out.

36
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:26,700
Fire!

37
00:09:31,450 --> 00:09:34,840
Ready your weapons!

38
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,170
Again!

39
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,100
We're ablaze on the right!

40
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:47,100
Keep formation!

41
00:09:50,810 --> 00:09:52,520
Pull!

42
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,530
Archers ready.

43
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:02,200
Release!

44
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,460
Nock!

45
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:12,830
Draw!

46
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:14,130
Loose!

47
00:10:21,050 --> 00:10:22,550
Archers!

48
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:32,160
Fire!

49
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:46,580
Raise the tower!
Raise the tower!

50
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:04,960
Back astern!
Back astern!

51
00:11:11,970 --> 00:11:13,890
Keep cranking.

52
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:25,730
Drop drawbridge!

53
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:27,490
The drawbridge is stuck!

54
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:38,460
Sir!

55
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,080
Loose!

56
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:55,400
Back.

57
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,580
Archers!

58
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:00,910
There!

59
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:02,210
Kill her!

60
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:04,220
Arishat!

61
00:14:14,450 --> 00:14:16,450
Arishat.

62
00:14:27,970 --> 00:14:31,890
Arishat!

63
00:14:38,930 --> 00:14:41,100
I'll wait for you.

64
00:15:24,110 --> 00:15:25,900
Check all the bodies!

65
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:27,890
Leave nothing!

66
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,420
I claim this city...

67
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,920
for the glory of Rome.

68
00:17:24,930 --> 00:17:26,930
<i>Vae victis.</i>

69
00:17:29,430 --> 00:17:31,230
Woe to the conquered.

70
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:50,250
...

71
00:17:50,250 --> 00:17:51,500
Next!

72
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:55,460
Move it!

73
00:18:10,770 --> 00:18:14,110
Down the stairs!
    Downstairs!

74
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:04,320
Hey.

75
00:19:04,330 --> 00:19:06,620
What damage have they
done you, eh?

76
00:19:19,370 --> 00:19:21,210
Lift it up. Easy, easy.

77
00:19:21,710 --> 00:19:23,710
Hold that.

78
00:19:29,850 --> 00:19:30,850
Arishat?

79
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:35,690
I am sorry, my son.

80
00:19:39,230 --> 00:19:40,730
I have not long.

81
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:44,110
This galley

82
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:46,620
is sailing us to something
I cannot endure.

83
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:49,990
I am ready... to be taken
to another place.

84
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:52,410
Stay here a while longer.

85
00:19:52,410 --> 00:19:53,910
...

86
00:19:55,410 --> 00:20:00,410
I remember well
when you first
were brought to us.

87
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:03,340
A lonely boy
from the desert.
Guileless.

88
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:04,810
Afraid.

89
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:08,840
You embraced everything
we taught you.

90
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:15,230
You found Arishat's love.
Your soul was replenished.

91
00:20:16,730 --> 00:20:19,980
When I die,

92
00:20:19,990 --> 00:20:22,780
my ancestors will meet me
in the next world.

93
00:20:24,770 --> 00:20:26,190
Who will meet you?

94
00:20:26,190 --> 00:20:28,610
Hanno,

95
00:20:28,610 --> 00:20:30,610
I am done.

96
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:34,110
Do not let them change
what you are.

97
00:21:00,730 --> 00:21:02,620
...

98
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:06,810
Have you seen this boy?

99
00:21:11,990 --> 00:21:14,370
Eama! Eama!

100
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:22,130
You must
go alone now, Hanno.

101
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,550
Never let them find you.

102
00:21:32,340 --> 00:21:34,220
Go. Go.

103
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:30,380
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

104
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:31,800
Emperor Geta.

105
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:35,890
Emperor Caracalla.

106
00:23:37,470 --> 00:23:39,110
General Acacius.

107
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:41,970
I have taken Numidia
in your names

108
00:23:42,470 --> 00:23:43,970
that your dominion
may eclipse that

109
00:23:43,970 --> 00:23:46,360
of every emperor
that came before you.

110
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:48,780
Crown him with laurels,
brother.

111
00:23:57,650 --> 00:24:00,950
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

112
00:24:06,710 --> 00:24:08,710
In honor
of your conquest,

113
00:24:09,710 --> 00:24:11,720
there will be games
in the Colosseum.

114
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:15,500
I require no games
in my honor.

115
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:18,810
Serving the Senate
and the people of Rome

116
00:24:19,310 --> 00:24:20,760
is honor enough for me.

117
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:23,680
You are too modest,
Acacius.

118
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:26,980
It does not suit a general
as accomplished as yourself.

119
00:24:29,320 --> 00:24:31,820
The glory is yours,
not mine.

120
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:35,320
I only ask for
some respite from war

121
00:24:35,320 --> 00:24:36,740
to spend time
with my wife.

122
00:24:36,740 --> 00:24:39,190
Your wife, yes.

123
00:24:39,190 --> 00:24:41,190
Remember the privileges
we have granted her?

124
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:44,660
Where is she now
to ignore such an occasion?

125
00:24:44,670 --> 00:24:47,510
There are victories
yet still to come.

126
00:24:49,170 --> 00:24:50,750
Persia.

127
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:52,960
India.

128
00:24:54,290 --> 00:24:57,710
Both... must be conquered.

129
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:02,550
Rome has so many subjects.

130
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:04,350
She must feed them.

131
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,850
They can eat war.

132
00:25:10,560 --> 00:25:13,980
Your triumphs
will be celebrated

133
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,980
as a tribute
to the greatness

134
00:25:17,980 --> 00:25:18,980
of the Roman people.

135
00:25:26,410 --> 00:25:29,410
...

136
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:42,820
Go to hell!

137
00:26:02,690 --> 00:26:05,080
Macrinus of Thysdrus,

138
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:07,580
master of gladiators!

139
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:29,890
...

140
00:26:29,890 --> 00:26:31,810
Stay close.

141
00:26:31,810 --> 00:26:34,310
...

142
00:26:48,070 --> 00:26:52,080
Aediles
and the town councilors,

143
00:26:52,580 --> 00:26:55,250
distinguished guests,

144
00:26:56,660 --> 00:26:58,470
citizens of Antium,

145
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,300
behold the fate

146
00:27:05,670 --> 00:27:08,340
of the conquered enemies
of Rome:

147
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:14,510
The barbarian Numidians
and their chieftain,

148
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:18,320
Jugurtha!

149
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:21,910
...

150
00:27:46,430 --> 00:27:49,130
...

151
00:28:38,320 --> 00:28:39,740
This one is interesting.

152
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:07,930
I'll buy him.

153
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:32,240
Halt! Who goes there?

154
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:34,880
General.

155
00:30:10,740 --> 00:30:12,080
My lady.

156
00:30:20,420 --> 00:30:22,700
I thank the gods
that brought you back home safe.

157
00:30:22,700 --> 00:30:26,040
Thank the Army.
They protected me.

158
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:28,840
Mm.

159
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:31,290
Let me feed you.

160
00:30:59,070 --> 00:31:00,070
Go.

161
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:02,090
To the wall.

162
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:15,390
The arena
is a sacred temple.

163
00:31:15,390 --> 00:31:17,340
For the bravest of you,

164
00:31:17,340 --> 00:31:20,340
the road to glory
runs through the arena.

165
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:22,350
The arena turns slaves
into gladiators

166
00:31:22,350 --> 00:31:24,180
and gladiators into free men.

167
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,190
You have worms.

168
00:31:36,990 --> 00:31:40,280
I know this one.
He eats monkeys.

169
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:56,880
Go. Sit. Eat.

170
00:32:57,490 --> 00:32:58,490
You.

171
00:32:59,860 --> 00:33:02,250
Hanno, get up.

172
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:12,590
What is
your native language?
I speak them all.

173
00:33:15,790 --> 00:33:19,180
You don't answer because
you can't or because you won't?

174
00:33:21,550 --> 00:33:22,470
Mm, all right.

175
00:33:22,470 --> 00:33:26,440
Violence...
is the universal language.

176
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:29,270
Viggo,
put him through his paces.

177
00:33:29,270 --> 00:33:33,110
He can fight an ape.
Let's see if he
can fight a man.

178
00:34:42,850 --> 00:34:44,350
Enough!

179
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,860
Very good.

180
00:34:51,220 --> 00:34:52,720
Very good.

181
00:34:54,730 --> 00:34:56,240
Hose him down.

182
00:34:59,810 --> 00:35:01,310
Bring him to me.

183
00:35:08,210 --> 00:35:09,630
Ah!

184
00:35:12,540 --> 00:35:14,540
A strong jaw.

185
00:35:16,050 --> 00:35:17,550
Good arms.

186
00:35:19,050 --> 00:35:20,550
Better smell.

187
00:35:23,420 --> 00:35:25,300
You will do well.

188
00:35:25,810 --> 00:35:27,670
It is an art,

189
00:35:27,680 --> 00:35:29,600
choosing gladiators.

190
00:35:31,100 --> 00:35:33,110
Some choose entertainers.

191
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:35,600
Some choose brute force.

192
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:37,020
I choose rage.

193
00:35:41,660 --> 00:35:42,670
Crowd loves blood.

194
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:44,660
And they love those who
love blood as much as they do.

195
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:47,660
And you, my friend, rage

196
00:35:48,160 --> 00:35:50,160
pours out of you like...

197
00:35:51,670 --> 00:35:53,180
like milk...

198
00:35:55,170 --> 00:35:56,420
from a whore's tit.

199
00:35:57,200 --> 00:35:59,210
You will be
quite the fighter.

200
00:35:59,210 --> 00:36:00,710
Not for you.

201
00:36:00,710 --> 00:36:03,010
You're right,
you do not fight for me.

202
00:36:03,010 --> 00:36:05,290
I put you in the ring,
you fight or you die.

203
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:06,810
The choice is yours.

204
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:09,800
But whose head
could I give you

205
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:13,270
that would satisfy this fury?

206
00:36:13,270 --> 00:36:15,270
The entire Roman Army's.

207
00:36:18,730 --> 00:36:20,070
Too much.

208
00:36:20,060 --> 00:36:21,890
Mm.

209
00:36:21,900 --> 00:36:23,910
The general will do.

210
00:36:23,900 --> 00:36:24,810
General?

211
00:36:26,230 --> 00:36:28,230
General Acacius?
                        Mm.

212
00:36:30,570 --> 00:36:32,910
Use your rage
in my service,

213
00:36:33,410 --> 00:36:36,910
and you will have his head
ready for your sword.

214
00:36:38,410 --> 00:36:41,410
Serve me and I will serve you.
Deny me...

215
00:36:42,720 --> 00:36:45,050
and you will die.

216
00:36:48,060 --> 00:36:50,070
There are times I wished
you'd abandoned me

217
00:36:50,060 --> 00:36:52,060
rather than
fight their wars.

218
00:36:52,060 --> 00:36:53,760
I've made my choice.

219
00:36:56,260 --> 00:36:57,730
I can live with it.

220
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:04,990
But my patience with those two
is at an end.

221
00:37:07,780 --> 00:37:10,040
Leta?

222
00:37:10,030 --> 00:37:13,580
You may go
to your quarters now.
We need nothing more.

223
00:37:20,590 --> 00:37:22,090
To hear wives and mothers
mourning their dead

224
00:37:22,590 --> 00:37:24,090
on that beach at Numidia...

225
00:37:26,590 --> 00:37:28,340
Lucilla.

226
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:34,680
No more.

227
00:37:37,190 --> 00:37:39,190
I will not waste

228
00:37:39,690 --> 00:37:43,190
another generation
of young men for their vanity.

229
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:48,710
If I fight another campaign,
it must be to depose them.

230
00:37:50,900 --> 00:37:52,740
When will your troops
arrive?

231
00:37:53,620 --> 00:37:55,960
They land at Ostia
in ten days.

232
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:59,830
How many of them will be
loyal to you alone?

233
00:38:01,830 --> 00:38:02,830
All of them.

234
00:38:05,130 --> 00:38:08,920
The emperors do not have
the support of the people.

235
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:13,420
The people are weary
of the madness, the tyranny.

236
00:38:16,430 --> 00:38:20,730
What is the dream of Rome
if her people are not free?

237
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:45,420
Enjoy yourself,
everyone,

238
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:47,420
to excess!

239
00:38:47,930 --> 00:38:50,770
Thank you. Thank you.

240
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:04,220
Oh!

241
00:39:04,730 --> 00:39:07,650
Please, drink.

242
00:39:07,650 --> 00:39:10,660
Ah! Excuse me. Macrinus!

243
00:39:12,150 --> 00:39:14,650
I knew the provinces
were not enough for you.

244
00:39:14,650 --> 00:39:18,150
I'm just here
                for the games.
Ah, well,

245
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,670
you won't be disappointed.

246
00:39:19,660 --> 00:39:23,160
Rome has all the games
that men like you like to play.

247
00:39:23,160 --> 00:39:25,160
Men like me, Thraex?
Men like us.

248
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:28,660
I know nothing happens
in Rome unless you've
tasted it first.

249
00:39:45,320 --> 00:39:47,080
What is my purpose here?

250
00:39:47,070 --> 00:39:48,350
You'll find out soon enough.

251
00:39:52,990 --> 00:39:55,440
What's this we hear
about you being interested

252
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:58,940
in standing for election
to the Senate, Macrinus?

253
00:39:59,450 --> 00:40:01,780
Me? No, I'm, uh...

254
00:40:01,780 --> 00:40:04,120
I don't even know how
to use an abacus.

255
00:40:04,620 --> 00:40:06,120
But I do understand that

256
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:08,620
it's customary
for your guests

257
00:40:08,620 --> 00:40:11,460
to make wagers
at these affairs?

258
00:40:11,460 --> 00:40:13,680
How large a sum
did you have in mind?

259
00:40:15,550 --> 00:40:16,890
A thousand gold denarii?

260
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:18,210
Two.

261
00:40:20,130 --> 00:40:21,630
Two?

262
00:40:23,140 --> 00:40:25,640
Denarii.

263
00:40:41,460 --> 00:40:44,330
Stand back! Stand back!

264
00:40:45,830 --> 00:40:47,290
My emperors.

265
00:40:47,290 --> 00:40:51,580
Lords, ladies and gentlemen,
and senators.

266
00:40:51,580 --> 00:40:53,920
For your entertainment,

267
00:40:54,420 --> 00:40:56,890
the art of combat!

268
00:40:59,340 --> 00:41:00,840
May I present

269
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:02,840
the barbarian versus,

270
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:07,230
from my own stable,
the mighty Vichek!

271
00:41:14,240 --> 00:41:17,240
This is your gladiator?
It is.

272
00:41:20,690 --> 00:41:23,080
Three rounds,
hand to hand.

273
00:41:23,080 --> 00:41:24,950
Swords!

274
00:41:24,950 --> 00:41:28,250
We want swords.
A fight to the death.

275
00:41:29,250 --> 00:41:32,540
No quarter to be offered...
or given.

276
00:41:32,540 --> 00:41:34,620
Fight now!

277
00:41:40,100 --> 00:41:41,100
Brother,

278
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:44,100
let's not kill each other
for their amusement.

279
00:42:50,580 --> 00:42:52,080
Remarkable!

280
00:42:54,590 --> 00:42:56,090
Remarkable!

281
00:42:57,040 --> 00:42:59,040
- Thraex, he looked expensive.
-

282
00:43:00,540 --> 00:43:03,050
Congratulations.
Thank you.

283
00:43:03,550 --> 00:43:05,050
Remarkable.

284
00:43:09,690 --> 00:43:11,100
From where do you hail?

285
00:43:16,980 --> 00:43:18,280
Speak.

286
00:43:21,780 --> 00:43:22,700
I said speak.

287
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:24,700
He is from the colonies,
Your Majesty.

288
00:43:25,200 --> 00:43:27,200
His native tongue
is all he understands.

289
00:43:33,710 --> 00:43:36,630
"The gates of hell
are open night and day.

290
00:43:38,630 --> 00:43:43,640
Smooth is the descent,
and easy is the way.

291
00:43:46,060 --> 00:43:48,470
But...

292
00:43:50,760 --> 00:43:52,560
to come back from hell

293
00:43:53,060 --> 00:43:54,560
and view the cheerful skies,

294
00:43:54,570 --> 00:43:59,530
in this the task
and mighty labor lies."

295
00:44:05,690 --> 00:44:07,030
Virgil, Your Majesty.

296
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:09,340
Poetry!

297
00:44:12,670 --> 00:44:15,120
Very clever, Macrinus.
Thank you.

298
00:44:16,620 --> 00:44:18,950
I've grown so bored,
but you surprise me.

299
00:44:18,960 --> 00:44:21,800
To amuse you is my only wish.

300
00:44:22,290 --> 00:44:23,760
We are amused,
we are amused.

301
00:44:25,760 --> 00:44:27,180
We are amused.

302
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:31,720
And we all look forward
to seeing your poet

303
00:44:32,720 --> 00:44:34,140
perform in the arena.

304
00:44:34,140 --> 00:44:37,110
As do I, Your Majesties.

305
00:44:38,110 --> 00:44:39,110
Thank you.

306
00:44:39,610 --> 00:44:40,480
Viggo?

307
00:44:41,900 --> 00:44:43,410
Come with me.

308
00:45:01,670 --> 00:45:03,980
You fought well today,
but you were lucky, too.

309
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:08,750
The lines you recited.

310
00:45:08,760 --> 00:45:11,520
You didn't learn that
in Africa, I know that.

311
00:45:12,310 --> 00:45:14,640
A good verse travels far.
                            Mm.

312
00:45:14,650 --> 00:45:16,490
Who taught you poetry?

313
00:45:16,980 --> 00:45:18,850
A captured Roman officer.

314
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:22,270
I was posted guard over him
and he used to tell us tales

315
00:45:22,270 --> 00:45:24,270
to pass the time.

316
00:45:25,270 --> 00:45:26,270
And what became
of this prisoner?

317
00:45:26,270 --> 00:45:27,770
Oh, we ate him.

318
00:45:29,280 --> 00:45:30,250
As barbarians do.

319
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:32,750
As barbarians do.

320
00:45:32,750 --> 00:45:34,750
And where were you born?

321
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:37,330
Why does my past matter
if it is my future

322
00:45:37,330 --> 00:45:39,330
to die for you in the arena?

323
00:45:46,540 --> 00:45:48,380
Tell me what use have I
for Roman money.

324
00:45:51,770 --> 00:45:53,280
A gladiator

325
00:45:54,270 --> 00:45:56,720
can buy his own freedom.
Mmm.

326
00:45:56,720 --> 00:45:58,720
His liberty.

327
00:45:59,720 --> 00:46:01,220
The Roman dream.

328
00:46:01,730 --> 00:46:03,740
No, the slave dreams
not of freedom

329
00:46:03,730 --> 00:46:06,030
but of a slave
to call his own.

330
00:46:07,030 --> 00:46:08,360
Cicero.

331
00:46:09,730 --> 00:46:12,230
Is that what you were
raised on, Macrinus?

332
00:46:13,540 --> 00:46:16,290
What did you have to do
for Roman money?

333
00:46:17,460 --> 00:46:19,160
You promised me a head.

334
00:46:19,160 --> 00:46:21,960
Earn your keep
and you can have
anyone's head.

335
00:46:46,240 --> 00:46:48,070
Father,

336
00:46:48,070 --> 00:46:50,440
protect us and guide us.

337
00:47:04,760 --> 00:47:05,760
Senators.

338
00:47:06,760 --> 00:47:07,760
My lady.

339
00:47:13,960 --> 00:47:17,470
My lady, I wish we were
meeting in better times.

340
00:47:17,970 --> 00:47:19,970
Better times will come.

341
00:47:21,470 --> 00:47:23,970
And why are we here?

342
00:47:23,970 --> 00:47:25,770
To take back the city.

343
00:47:27,610 --> 00:47:31,060
And restore Rome
to where she should be.

344
00:47:32,530 --> 00:47:34,530
An exciting venture.

345
00:47:35,540 --> 00:47:38,050
When?
On the final day
of the games.

346
00:47:39,040 --> 00:47:42,040
My army waits for my command
at Ostia.

347
00:47:42,040 --> 00:47:44,540
Five thousand soldiers
loyal to me...

348
00:47:46,050 --> 00:47:48,810
will enter Rome
and then the Colosseum,

349
00:47:48,800 --> 00:47:50,800
where they will
arrest the emperors

350
00:47:50,800 --> 00:47:52,220
for their crimes
against the Senate

351
00:47:53,170 --> 00:47:54,670
and their people.

352
00:47:55,590 --> 00:48:00,840
Uh, this plan
is ambitious and risky.

353
00:48:00,840 --> 00:48:03,350
Rome will be yours
to administer and to--

354
00:48:03,850 --> 00:48:08,100
Marcus Aurelius talked
of restoring power
to the Senate,

355
00:48:08,600 --> 00:48:12,600
but that was a generation ago.
Much has changed.

356
00:48:12,610 --> 00:48:16,620
The people
have not seen hope

357
00:48:16,610 --> 00:48:18,080
for many years.

358
00:48:18,080 --> 00:48:21,950
But with time...
and guidance...

359
00:48:23,330 --> 00:48:26,840
Lucilla, you are the daughter
of Marcus Aurelius.

360
00:48:27,340 --> 00:48:29,340
He had my loyalty.

361
00:48:30,840 --> 00:48:32,760
And so do you.

362
00:48:35,180 --> 00:48:36,550
Senator Thraex?

363
00:48:38,430 --> 00:48:41,770
Politics follows power,
my lady.

364
00:48:42,770 --> 00:48:46,100
Take back
what is rightfully yours...

365
00:48:47,110 --> 00:48:48,940
and the Senate
will support you.

366
00:48:50,280 --> 00:48:51,280
Thank you.

367
00:49:07,240 --> 00:49:08,660
Food! Food!

368
00:49:13,580 --> 00:49:15,880
When I was told of this place,

369
00:49:15,890 --> 00:49:18,010
they never mentioned
the stink.

370
00:49:19,840 --> 00:49:21,310
That would be Hanno.

371
00:49:24,430 --> 00:49:27,150
Well, you'll have to
put up with me as I am.

372
00:49:32,740 --> 00:49:35,750
And what's that up there?
A wolf?

373
00:49:37,660 --> 00:49:40,660
The twins there,
they were outcasts.

374
00:49:40,660 --> 00:49:42,440
Left in the hills to die.

375
00:49:43,780 --> 00:49:47,330
That wolf found them
and she suckled them
on her milk.

376
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:51,180
Raised by an animal.
It's in their blood.

377
00:49:51,170 --> 00:49:53,960
How do you know this place?

378
00:49:55,430 --> 00:49:57,440
I know the chaos
they brought.

379
00:49:58,430 --> 00:50:01,300
This city infects
everything it touches.

380
00:50:01,300 --> 00:50:03,680
I never dreamt
it would be so big.

381
00:50:03,680 --> 00:50:05,180
Don't fall for it.

382
00:50:05,190 --> 00:50:07,200
This city is diseased.

383
00:50:08,610 --> 00:50:11,030
Food! Food!

384
00:50:34,550 --> 00:50:36,970
You! Barbarian scum!

385
00:50:38,390 --> 00:50:40,900
...

386
00:50:42,810 --> 00:50:44,770
Help me.
Please, help me!

387
00:51:21,630 --> 00:51:22,960
Ah!
            Thraex.

388
00:51:26,720 --> 00:51:27,630
About our wager.

389
00:51:28,130 --> 00:51:29,430
Ah. The barbarian.

390
00:51:29,940 --> 00:51:31,220
Yes, I haven't forgotten,
I always repay my debts.

391
00:51:31,220 --> 00:51:33,020
I was merely
going to suggest

392
00:51:33,020 --> 00:51:35,020
that perhaps your luck
might change.

393
00:51:35,030 --> 00:51:37,490
Shall we say
double or quits?

394
00:51:41,950 --> 00:51:43,450
Ah.
                    Ah.

395
00:51:55,750 --> 00:51:57,060
Get back!

396
00:52:11,260 --> 00:52:12,760
Fresh meat.

397
00:52:16,680 --> 00:52:18,680
Line up! Line up!

398
00:52:49,180 --> 00:52:52,130
Play! Play!

399
00:53:07,070 --> 00:53:09,570
Emperor Caracalla.

400
00:53:10,070 --> 00:53:12,070
Emperor Geta.

401
00:53:12,070 --> 00:53:14,910
Citizens of Rome!

402
00:53:16,710 --> 00:53:19,540
These sacred games

403
00:53:20,050 --> 00:53:23,000
are held to honor
the victory of Rome

404
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:26,500
over the barbarians of Numidia.

405
00:53:27,420 --> 00:53:29,890
Go! Go!

406
00:53:32,810 --> 00:53:36,310
And to honor
Rome's legionary commander,

407
00:53:36,810 --> 00:53:38,730
General Justus Acacius!

408
00:53:38,730 --> 00:53:41,570
Long live Acacius!

409
00:53:41,570 --> 00:53:42,900
And with him

410
00:53:42,900 --> 00:53:47,910
Lucilla, the daughter
of Emperor Marcus Aurelius.

411
00:53:49,910 --> 00:53:53,410
- Lucilla!
- Mother of Rome!

412
00:53:54,160 --> 00:53:55,450
Acacius.

413
00:53:55,950 --> 00:53:57,250
General.

414
00:54:04,710 --> 00:54:07,880
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

415
00:54:08,460 --> 00:54:13,270
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

416
00:54:14,180 --> 00:54:15,180
Speak to them.

417
00:54:15,690 --> 00:54:17,700
Speak to us!

418
00:54:26,030 --> 00:54:28,900
I am not an orator

419
00:54:28,900 --> 00:54:30,400
or a politician.

420
00:54:31,900 --> 00:54:33,400
I am a soldier.

421
00:54:35,910 --> 00:54:41,090
I have seen bravery
in men and women during war.

422
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:43,550
And even once in this arena.

423
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:46,880
So if you ask anything
of the gods...

424
00:54:48,750 --> 00:54:51,250
ask for that same bravery.

425
00:54:53,590 --> 00:54:55,510
Because Rome needs it now.

426
00:54:59,560 --> 00:55:02,600
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

427
00:55:02,600 --> 00:55:06,100
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

428
00:55:18,530 --> 00:55:20,830
From the South Gate,

429
00:55:21,330 --> 00:55:26,170
fighters from the stable
of Macrinus of Thysdrus!

430
00:55:38,640 --> 00:55:40,810
From the stables

431
00:55:40,800 --> 00:55:44,610
of Emperors Caracalla
and Geta themselves,

432
00:55:44,610 --> 00:55:46,860
the undefeated champion:

433
00:55:47,360 --> 00:55:50,780
Glyceo the Destroyer!

434
00:55:57,570 --> 00:55:58,400
Hold.

435
00:56:21,010 --> 00:56:23,010
Hold.

436
00:56:24,310 --> 00:56:25,980
Hail Caesars!

437
00:56:27,600 --> 00:56:30,900
Glyceo! Glyceo! Glyceo!

438
00:56:42,670 --> 00:56:45,960
Hold together
and when it charges,
break for the wall.

439
00:56:45,950 --> 00:56:46,790
Why should I?

440
00:56:51,170 --> 00:56:51,960
Hold!

441
00:56:53,090 --> 00:56:54,260
Hold!

442
00:56:54,260 --> 00:56:55,260
Break!

443
00:56:56,210 --> 00:56:57,510
Cowards!

444
00:57:06,940 --> 00:57:08,110
...

445
00:57:11,610 --> 00:57:13,730
To the wall!

446
00:57:25,540 --> 00:57:26,540
Come on!

447
00:59:10,060 --> 00:59:13,150
Brother, it's that poet,
is it not?

448
00:59:13,650 --> 00:59:15,650
I can't remember.

449
00:59:15,650 --> 00:59:17,650
That night was a blur.

450
00:59:19,160 --> 00:59:21,580
"The gates of hell
are open night and day.

451
00:59:21,570 --> 00:59:24,990
Smooth the desc--"
I forget.

452
00:59:24,990 --> 00:59:26,490
"Smooth the descent..."

453
00:59:27,500 --> 00:59:29,500
"Smooth is the descent,

454
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:32,000
easy is the way."

455
00:59:39,460 --> 00:59:40,260
Shield!

456
01:00:16,550 --> 01:00:20,090
Mercy! Mercy! Mercy!

457
01:00:22,000 --> 01:00:23,250
Blood.

458
01:00:26,060 --> 01:00:27,570
Lucilla,

459
01:00:28,060 --> 01:00:29,390
shall we show mercy?

460
01:00:29,390 --> 01:00:31,090
Mercy.

461
01:00:46,330 --> 01:00:48,540
No mercy!

462
01:00:48,530 --> 01:00:50,330
Your life has been
spared by the gods--

463
01:00:50,330 --> 01:00:54,580
I would sooner face your blade
than accept Roman mercy!

464
01:01:10,600 --> 01:01:13,940
Kill! Kill! Kill!

465
01:01:13,940 --> 01:01:17,440
Kill! Kill! Kill!

466
01:01:28,650 --> 01:01:33,570
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

467
01:02:02,100 --> 01:02:04,400
The road to freedom
doesn't run
through the arena.

468
01:02:05,400 --> 01:02:06,940
It leads to this.

469
01:02:11,330 --> 01:02:13,190
Go to your cells.

470
01:02:17,450 --> 01:02:20,950
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

471
01:02:37,850 --> 01:02:38,850
Come on, let's go.

472
01:02:52,150 --> 01:02:55,490
"Gates of hell
are open night and day.

473
01:02:56,320 --> 01:02:58,320
Smooth is the descent...

474
01:02:58,320 --> 01:03:00,160
...easy is the way."

475
01:03:04,160 --> 01:03:06,660
<i>There, there, there, there.</i>

476
01:03:06,670 --> 01:03:08,180
<i>And I've got you.</i>

477
01:03:08,170 --> 01:03:10,720
<i>I'm Maximus,
the savior of Rome!</i>

478
01:03:30,490 --> 01:03:32,360
Scatto and Argento.

479
01:03:46,170 --> 01:03:47,510
Lucius is safe?

480
01:04:05,220 --> 01:04:06,610
Lucius!

481
01:04:19,040 --> 01:04:20,960
Lucius,

482
01:04:20,960 --> 01:04:23,880
you're the sole heir
to the throne now.

483
01:04:25,880 --> 01:04:26,880
There are men
who want to kill you

484
01:04:27,380 --> 01:04:28,660
so they can take power.

485
01:04:30,500 --> 01:04:33,470
I promise I'll bring you back
as soon as it's safe.

486
01:04:33,470 --> 01:04:37,470
Mother, why can't you
come with me?

487
01:04:37,470 --> 01:04:39,970
I... I have to
stay here for your sake.

488
01:04:39,980 --> 01:04:41,900
And for the sake of Rome.

489
01:04:41,890 --> 01:04:44,310
Remember who you are.

490
01:04:44,810 --> 01:04:46,310
And that I love you.

491
01:04:47,320 --> 01:04:48,820
I love you.

492
01:04:49,320 --> 01:04:50,570
Come.

493
01:04:53,770 --> 01:04:55,270
Give me your leg.

494
01:04:56,780 --> 01:04:58,700
Go. Go!

495
01:05:05,450 --> 01:05:06,950
So...

496
01:05:10,370 --> 01:05:11,870
What's your name?

497
01:05:14,590 --> 01:05:17,090
I'm Ravi. I'm a doctor.

498
01:05:18,100 --> 01:05:21,600
Because... more men die
of infected wounds

499
01:05:22,100 --> 01:05:24,600
than out there, in the arena.

500
01:05:25,860 --> 01:05:28,650
This needs to be cleaned,
it needs to be stitched and

501
01:05:28,640 --> 01:05:31,360
it is going to hurt.

502
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:32,690
Mm.

503
01:05:32,700 --> 01:05:36,070
This is Devil's Breath
and opium.

504
01:05:36,570 --> 01:05:38,080
It's for the pain.

505
01:05:39,070 --> 01:05:40,570
You should breathe in.

506
01:05:46,830 --> 01:05:48,220
I've been here
so long now,

507
01:05:48,210 --> 01:05:50,580
I don't even notice anymore.

508
01:05:51,080 --> 01:05:53,580
I've done more amputations
than I can count.

509
01:05:54,550 --> 01:05:57,550
Where'd you
            learn your trade?
Why do you ask?

510
01:05:57,550 --> 01:05:59,000
You've got a heavy hand.

511
01:06:00,470 --> 01:06:01,970
I used to be
a gladiator myself.

512
01:06:01,970 --> 01:06:03,310
Ah.

513
01:06:03,310 --> 01:06:05,640
And would you have bested me?

514
01:06:05,640 --> 01:06:07,090
In your prime, of course.

515
01:06:08,600 --> 01:06:11,070
In your current state,
I could best you now.

516
01:06:13,020 --> 01:06:16,020
Luckily for you,
I have put down my sword.

517
01:06:16,020 --> 01:06:18,520
So now I spend my days

518
01:06:18,520 --> 01:06:21,030
saving lives
instead of taking them.

519
01:06:22,780 --> 01:06:25,280
And why such a change
so late in life?

520
01:06:25,780 --> 01:06:28,280
What we do in life

521
01:06:28,280 --> 01:06:30,700
echoes in eternity.

522
01:06:34,620 --> 01:06:36,120
I feel like
I know those words.

523
01:06:36,130 --> 01:06:38,600
I can't take credit.

524
01:06:38,590 --> 01:06:41,100
It's written on
one of the tombs.

525
01:06:41,600 --> 01:06:44,020
Over the bones of a gladiator.

526
01:06:44,020 --> 01:06:45,470
My champion!

527
01:06:45,470 --> 01:06:47,940
I smell Devil's Breath!

528
01:06:50,440 --> 01:06:53,440
My... champion.

529
01:06:54,440 --> 01:06:56,280
Did you hear that crowd?

530
01:06:59,110 --> 01:07:01,320
Did you hear that crowd?
                        Mm-hm.

531
01:07:03,200 --> 01:07:05,620
You have something.
I knew it from the start.

532
01:07:05,620 --> 01:07:09,540
Did you now?
Yes. The Greeks call it...

533
01:07:10,540 --> 01:07:12,040
<i>thymos.</i>

534
01:07:12,040 --> 01:07:13,540
Smoke.

535
01:07:14,050 --> 01:07:15,550
Rage.

536
01:07:16,550 --> 01:07:18,420
That rage is your gift.

537
01:07:19,340 --> 01:07:22,100
Like the great Achilles.

538
01:07:22,090 --> 01:07:24,390
Never let it go.

539
01:07:24,390 --> 01:07:27,310
It will carry you
to greatness,

540
01:07:27,310 --> 01:07:29,260
my champion.

541
01:07:48,610 --> 01:07:50,660
Thank you

542
01:07:50,670 --> 01:07:52,680
for inviting me.

543
01:07:53,170 --> 01:07:54,950
This is truly an honor.

544
01:07:59,760 --> 01:08:01,760
I hear you are
the talk of the court.

545
01:08:04,130 --> 01:08:05,130
Yes.

546
01:08:06,130 --> 01:08:07,630
We've met before.

547
01:08:08,130 --> 01:08:10,130
Have we?
Long ago.

548
01:08:11,640 --> 01:08:13,140
Where?

549
01:08:13,640 --> 01:08:15,140
I was in the service
of your father's army

550
01:08:15,640 --> 01:08:17,640
on his African campaign.

551
01:08:18,640 --> 01:08:20,640
You served
with my father?

552
01:08:24,650 --> 01:08:25,650
Mm.

553
01:08:26,120 --> 01:08:28,570
I had the privilege

554
01:08:29,570 --> 01:08:31,070
of reading
his "Meditations."

555
01:08:31,070 --> 01:08:32,320
Mm.

556
01:08:35,130 --> 01:08:37,130
"The best revenge

557
01:08:38,630 --> 01:08:41,500
is to be unlike him
who performed the injury."

558
01:08:43,920 --> 01:08:46,340
I hear you've been
arming half the legions

559
01:08:46,340 --> 01:08:51,760
in the entire empire,
and here, now, in Rome...

560
01:08:52,760 --> 01:08:55,730
you're gaining influence
by sponsoring gladiators.

561
01:08:55,730 --> 01:08:58,020
I do it for the love
of the sport.

562
01:08:58,020 --> 01:09:01,100
And where did you find
these gladiators?

563
01:09:01,900 --> 01:09:04,910
They're usually
prisoners of war.

564
01:09:05,690 --> 01:09:09,030
Or vagrants.
Why do you ask?

565
01:09:09,530 --> 01:09:12,030
A man can choose to fight...

566
01:09:13,780 --> 01:09:15,280
and stay alive.

567
01:09:15,280 --> 01:09:18,870
It's the same in life as it is
in the arena, is it not?

568
01:09:21,120 --> 01:09:22,960
Who is this?

569
01:09:22,960 --> 01:09:25,340
That is my father
as a youth.

570
01:09:28,430 --> 01:09:29,850
<i>She had a child?</i>

571
01:09:29,850 --> 01:09:31,770
Mm.

572
01:09:31,770 --> 01:09:34,270
It's common knowledge.
When Commodus was killed,

573
01:09:34,270 --> 01:09:36,270
the boy disappeared.
                Mm.

574
01:09:36,270 --> 01:09:38,270
But who would care?
            Lucilla would care.

575
01:09:38,270 --> 01:09:40,860
More wine!
More wine!

576
01:09:42,360 --> 01:09:45,860
He was of the royal bloodline,
after all.

577
01:09:47,370 --> 01:09:48,880
And his father?

578
01:09:48,870 --> 01:09:53,870
Ostensibly,
Lucius Verus.

579
01:09:53,870 --> 01:09:55,370
See, it was
an arranged marriage.

580
01:09:55,870 --> 01:09:56,740
She was 14.

581
01:09:56,740 --> 01:10:00,130
Mm.
    Females were not his taste.

582
01:10:00,130 --> 01:10:01,630
Nor mine, some days.
                Nor yours!

583
01:10:03,000 --> 01:10:07,380
No, no, no.
By rumor, you see,
she took lovers.

584
01:10:07,890 --> 01:10:11,890
And by rumor,
the real father...
was Commodus.

585
01:10:12,730 --> 01:10:15,100
Brotherly love,
you see?
                Yeah.

586
01:10:15,590 --> 01:10:17,090
If he died,

587
01:10:18,100 --> 01:10:20,600
there has to be remains.
Mm.

588
01:10:20,600 --> 01:10:24,100
And if he lived,
that would make him about...

589
01:10:24,100 --> 01:10:26,020
Um, well,
let's work it out.

590
01:10:26,020 --> 01:10:29,440
He was about 12
                when he died?
Yes.

591
01:10:29,440 --> 01:10:34,080
So that would make him...

592
01:11:09,730 --> 01:11:10,230
My lady.

593
01:11:11,230 --> 01:11:11,730
Gracchus.

594
01:11:13,240 --> 01:11:15,080
Please come.
Thank you.

595
01:11:33,920 --> 01:11:34,920
Gladiator...

596
01:11:36,430 --> 01:11:37,690
do you know me?

597
01:11:46,150 --> 01:11:47,650
Do you have a family?

598
01:11:50,160 --> 01:11:53,030
A wife. Arishat.

599
01:11:54,940 --> 01:11:55,780
Arishat.

600
01:11:56,030 --> 01:11:59,450
She was killed
under your husband's command.

601
01:12:02,280 --> 01:12:04,250
Rome drowns
in its own blood.

602
01:12:04,250 --> 01:12:06,620
And yet you enjoy
the pleasures of the Colosseum.

603
01:12:08,040 --> 01:12:10,870
There is much
you do not understand.

604
01:12:17,770 --> 01:12:18,630
Lucius.

605
01:12:18,970 --> 01:12:21,050
I do not know
who you think I am.

606
01:12:23,560 --> 01:12:25,070
My name is Hanno,

607
01:12:25,560 --> 01:12:27,560
and I have no mother,
or none that I can remember.

608
01:12:34,570 --> 01:12:36,450
I'm so sorry.

609
01:12:36,450 --> 01:12:38,870
If your son were here,
I feel sure he would tell you

610
01:12:38,870 --> 01:12:40,870
not to grieve him.

611
01:12:40,870 --> 01:12:42,370
For he would not be the boy
that you sent away.

612
01:12:42,880 --> 01:12:44,640
That boy is dead.

613
01:12:46,910 --> 01:12:48,910
You may think
I have little worth.

614
01:12:50,920 --> 01:12:52,930
You may think
I betrayed you.

615
01:12:54,920 --> 01:12:56,420
But I need you to know...

616
01:12:57,920 --> 01:13:00,920
if you will not have
your mother's love,

617
01:13:00,930 --> 01:13:03,940
then take
your father's strength.

618
01:13:04,930 --> 01:13:06,430
You need it.

619
01:13:08,930 --> 01:13:13,070
His name was
Maximus Decimus Meridius.

620
01:13:14,570 --> 01:13:15,570
And I see him in you.

621
01:13:16,070 --> 01:13:17,070
Get out.

622
01:13:19,360 --> 01:13:21,700
My lady, we must go at once!

623
01:13:25,200 --> 01:13:27,700
Lucius, you were loved

624
01:13:27,700 --> 01:13:31,210
by myself
and by your father.

625
01:13:32,210 --> 01:13:33,620
Your name
was on his lips--

626
01:13:33,630 --> 01:13:35,600
Get out!

627
01:14:01,400 --> 01:14:03,370
Lucius is alive.

628
01:14:05,870 --> 01:14:07,710
Are you certain?

629
01:14:07,710 --> 01:14:09,080
Yes.

630
01:14:10,080 --> 01:14:11,380
I know my son.

631
01:14:14,220 --> 01:14:16,230
I spoke to him
tonight.

632
01:14:19,670 --> 01:14:22,670
He may be lost to me
for what I did,

633
01:14:24,180 --> 01:14:25,600
but he lives.

634
01:14:27,060 --> 01:14:29,560
The third day of the games
is tomorrow.

635
01:14:29,560 --> 01:14:31,060
Most fighters won't survive.

636
01:14:31,070 --> 01:14:32,580
Acacius,

637
01:14:34,070 --> 01:14:35,440
you must help him.

638
01:14:36,360 --> 01:14:38,200
- Help him?
-              Yes.

639
01:14:40,530 --> 01:14:43,540
I failed him then.

640
01:14:44,030 --> 01:14:45,530
I know I did.

641
01:14:47,030 --> 01:14:49,030
I cannot fail him now.

642
01:14:52,040 --> 01:14:53,370
The army is in Ostia.

643
01:14:53,370 --> 01:14:56,210
If we wait a few days...

644
01:14:56,210 --> 01:14:58,210
He could be dead
by then.

645
01:15:00,210 --> 01:15:01,630
Acacius,

646
01:15:01,630 --> 01:15:05,600
I would willingly
give my life for Rome,

647
01:15:06,600 --> 01:15:08,970
but I will not
give my son's.

648
01:15:15,030 --> 01:15:17,390
And one.

649
01:15:18,310 --> 01:15:20,110
And two.

650
01:15:20,370 --> 01:15:22,960
And one.

651
01:15:22,950 --> 01:15:25,950
Together.
Timing, timing, timing!

652
01:15:26,960 --> 01:15:30,470
And one. And two.

653
01:15:30,790 --> 01:15:32,910
And one.

654
01:15:32,910 --> 01:15:34,660
Pause, pause!

655
01:15:37,920 --> 01:15:38,920
We won't get far
like this.

656
01:15:40,420 --> 01:15:42,920
Just him. You go.

657
01:15:42,920 --> 01:15:44,920
Go!

658
01:15:44,920 --> 01:15:48,430
Let's see how far you can go
on your own without your team.

659
01:15:49,930 --> 01:15:51,730
Ready?

660
01:15:51,730 --> 01:15:53,010
One!

661
01:15:54,020 --> 01:15:54,860
And two!

662
01:15:54,850 --> 01:15:57,180
Timing, timing!

663
01:15:57,690 --> 01:15:59,000
Come on, more!

664
01:16:04,240 --> 01:16:05,740
More!

665
01:16:22,760 --> 01:16:23,960
Leave him.

666
01:16:42,700 --> 01:16:46,150
It's just vinegar,
my friend.

667
01:16:48,150 --> 01:16:50,650
There will be
no more opium for you.

668
01:16:52,160 --> 01:16:55,630
There is plenty of pain waiting
for you in the next life.

669
01:16:56,130 --> 01:16:59,130
I don't know why
you are so greedy for it
in this one.

670
01:17:04,140 --> 01:17:05,650
Are you a free man, Ravi?

671
01:17:05,640 --> 01:17:07,140
"Free."

672
01:17:09,310 --> 01:17:11,310
I am. Mm.

673
01:17:11,810 --> 01:17:13,180
I laid down my sword

674
01:17:13,180 --> 01:17:15,310
and I swore never
to pick it up again.

675
01:17:15,310 --> 01:17:17,100
And yet
you choose this hell?

676
01:17:17,100 --> 01:17:18,600
Mm-hm.

677
01:17:18,600 --> 01:17:19,980
What was your home before?

678
01:17:21,350 --> 01:17:22,850
Varanasi.

679
01:17:22,850 --> 01:17:25,160
And why don't you go back?

680
01:17:25,160 --> 01:17:26,690
I wish I could.

681
01:17:26,690 --> 01:17:28,490
But...
                Eh-eh-eh.

682
01:17:30,910 --> 01:17:32,860
I met a woman.
Ah.

683
01:17:33,870 --> 01:17:36,260
It's always a woman.
                Always.

684
01:17:36,250 --> 01:17:40,420
She is from Londinium.
Britannia. You know.

685
01:17:40,420 --> 01:17:42,170
So now...

686
01:17:42,170 --> 01:17:45,130
our sons,
they speak only Latin.

687
01:17:45,630 --> 01:17:47,630
My daughter's eyes,
they are as blue as yours.

688
01:17:50,630 --> 01:17:51,880
We are Romans now.

689
01:17:51,880 --> 01:17:55,690
I grew up hearing stories
at my grandfather's knee.

690
01:17:56,970 --> 01:18:00,310
He used to talk
of the dream that was Rome.

691
01:18:02,690 --> 01:18:06,700
It was so fragile,
you could only whisper it...

692
01:18:08,700 --> 01:18:10,700
or it would vanish.

693
01:18:11,540 --> 01:18:12,870
So,

694
01:18:13,370 --> 01:18:14,740
what was this dream?

695
01:18:14,740 --> 01:18:19,660
A Rome where all could live
under fair law and be protected.

696
01:18:20,660 --> 01:18:22,160
A Rome of the Senate.

697
01:18:24,170 --> 01:18:25,680
A Rome of hope.

698
01:18:28,390 --> 01:18:32,840
Your grandfather,
he sounds like
a dangerous man.

699
01:18:32,840 --> 01:18:34,310
Hm.

700
01:18:37,150 --> 01:18:39,160
The odds are against you.

701
01:18:41,650 --> 01:18:43,650
The odds
are always against me.

702
01:18:44,650 --> 01:18:45,570
Don't worry, old man.

703
01:18:45,570 --> 01:18:47,520
Eh?

704
01:18:51,030 --> 01:18:53,040
You should
            get some rest. Hm?
Mm.

705
01:18:54,530 --> 01:18:56,530
Your men will need you
to lead them tomorrow.

706
01:19:13,270 --> 01:19:14,690
This is about survival.

707
01:19:16,130 --> 01:19:17,130
Survive!

708
01:19:17,140 --> 01:19:21,060
In the name of Poseidon,

709
01:19:21,060 --> 01:19:25,400
we celebrate the glory
of naval war.

710
01:19:25,390 --> 01:19:27,280
They have archers.

711
01:19:27,280 --> 01:19:29,700
Be ready.
Listen for my commands.

712
01:19:29,700 --> 01:19:32,570
Stay together
and pull as one, yes?

713
01:19:32,570 --> 01:19:33,450
Yes!

714
01:19:33,450 --> 01:19:35,900
Yes?
Yes!

715
01:19:42,990 --> 01:19:45,460
Today we relive

716
01:19:45,460 --> 01:19:49,250
the Battle of Salamis!

717
01:19:50,590 --> 01:19:55,100
The Trojans
versus the Persians!

718
01:19:59,480 --> 01:20:01,180
- Oars out!
- Oars!

719
01:20:02,010 --> 01:20:04,150
And... pull!

720
01:20:23,450 --> 01:20:25,920
Archers!

721
01:20:25,920 --> 01:20:26,700
Archers!

722
01:20:28,840 --> 01:20:29,920
Pull!

723
01:20:38,930 --> 01:20:40,430
Pull!

724
01:20:43,220 --> 01:20:44,300
Pull!

725
01:20:57,370 --> 01:20:59,790
Pull! To my time!

726
01:21:00,740 --> 01:21:01,990
And... now!

727
01:21:04,790 --> 01:21:06,990
Left side! Ready, and

728
01:21:07,000 --> 01:21:09,090
ship oars now!

729
01:21:09,080 --> 01:21:11,410
Oars in! Oars in!

730
01:21:12,670 --> 01:21:13,720
Get down!

731
01:21:29,650 --> 01:21:33,770
And pull! And pull!

732
01:21:36,410 --> 01:21:38,610
Don't stop!

733
01:21:41,080 --> 01:21:42,080
Pull!

734
01:21:44,580 --> 01:21:46,000
And right!

735
01:21:51,620 --> 01:21:53,340
Ready to ram!

736
01:21:55,430 --> 01:21:58,040
And brace! Brace!

737
01:22:37,970 --> 01:22:39,250
Everyone regroup!

738
01:23:15,620 --> 01:23:17,760
Praetorians!

739
01:23:18,930 --> 01:23:21,210
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

740
01:23:21,800 --> 01:23:22,630
Move, move.

741
01:23:29,390 --> 01:23:32,720
In the name of the emperors...

742
01:23:32,720 --> 01:23:37,360
the victor is Hanno!

743
01:23:49,040 --> 01:23:50,790
Who did this?

744
01:23:53,630 --> 01:23:55,880
Who did this?!

745
01:23:56,750 --> 01:23:58,250
It was me!
I did it!

746
01:23:58,250 --> 01:24:00,630
I did it!
I did it! I did it!
It was me!

747
01:24:05,170 --> 01:24:07,590
Geta will want retribution
for all of you.

748
01:24:08,590 --> 01:24:09,590
Did you learn to shoot
in the same place

749
01:24:09,590 --> 01:24:11,390
you learned to recite poetry?

750
01:24:11,400 --> 01:24:12,190
Be glad it wasn't me,

751
01:24:12,680 --> 01:24:14,180
or that arrow
would have found you.

752
01:24:29,750 --> 01:24:31,160
Be seated.

753
01:24:33,620 --> 01:24:35,090
I have news for you.

754
01:24:39,670 --> 01:24:41,170
He's here, sir.

755
01:24:44,210 --> 01:24:46,350
Oh, still here.

756
01:24:48,630 --> 01:24:49,630
Macrinus.

757
01:24:50,130 --> 01:24:52,190
Welcome.

758
01:24:53,690 --> 01:24:56,190
Yes, I'm listening.

759
01:24:56,190 --> 01:24:58,610
You know
this is my house now.

760
01:24:58,610 --> 01:25:01,030
Your debt to me is
over 10,000 denarii.

761
01:25:01,030 --> 01:25:02,360
You know that.

762
01:25:02,360 --> 01:25:05,200
I have other things. Uh...

763
01:25:05,200 --> 01:25:07,070
Cattle. Art!

764
01:25:07,070 --> 01:25:08,820
Truth, then.

765
01:25:08,820 --> 01:25:10,700
What do you... want?

766
01:25:10,710 --> 01:25:13,170
Truth.
That's what I want.

767
01:25:13,160 --> 01:25:17,630
Nothing happens in Rome
without your knowledge.

768
01:25:19,130 --> 01:25:21,130
You have
the senators' trust.

769
01:25:21,630 --> 01:25:24,130
You have
Lucilla's trust.

770
01:25:24,140 --> 01:25:26,650
More importantly,
you have my trust.

771
01:25:28,640 --> 01:25:32,890
You wish my... loyalty?

772
01:25:32,890 --> 01:25:34,680
I own...

773
01:25:36,180 --> 01:25:37,680
your house.

774
01:25:38,180 --> 01:25:40,680
I want your loyalty.

775
01:25:44,410 --> 01:25:45,750
I...

776
01:25:47,080 --> 01:25:48,840
Tell me.
I have heard...

777
01:25:48,830 --> 01:25:51,610
of a plot...

778
01:25:52,610 --> 01:25:55,110
to dethrone the emperors.
                    Yes.

779
01:25:55,120 --> 01:25:57,630
But the plan
has been delayed, uh...

780
01:25:57,620 --> 01:26:00,620
A gladiator is to be rescued
from the arena.

781
01:26:01,120 --> 01:26:02,420
Tonight.
            Mm.

782
01:26:02,420 --> 01:26:05,760
I don't know why.
        I know why. I know who.

783
01:26:07,760 --> 01:26:09,050
Pack.

784
01:26:12,880 --> 01:26:14,380
Quickly.

785
01:26:41,960 --> 01:26:43,300
Open up!

786
01:27:03,480 --> 01:27:05,490
Open for
the emperors' guard!

787
01:27:33,010 --> 01:27:36,520
My Lady, come with us.

788
01:28:21,680 --> 01:28:24,060
Thanks to the civic virtue

789
01:28:24,070 --> 01:28:26,780
of men like Thraex
and Macrinus,

790
01:28:27,740 --> 01:28:29,750
your insurrection

791
01:28:30,190 --> 01:28:32,160
has been revealed.

792
01:28:34,160 --> 01:28:35,660
The honor,

793
01:28:36,660 --> 01:28:40,450
the dignitas that Rome
has bestowed upon you...

794
01:28:42,780 --> 01:28:45,790
all this you have forfeited
by your treachery.

795
01:28:46,290 --> 01:28:48,290
Please, Emperor Geta.

796
01:28:48,670 --> 01:28:50,540
Torture me if you want,

797
01:28:51,540 --> 01:28:52,930
but do not lecture me.

798
01:28:52,930 --> 01:28:56,300
Your name
will be forgotten!

799
01:28:57,800 --> 01:29:00,800
Lost... to history.

800
01:29:02,800 --> 01:29:03,800
You are damned,
General.

801
01:29:06,810 --> 01:29:08,610
You laugh.
 You damn me?

802
01:29:09,940 --> 01:29:11,280
I don't care.

803
01:29:11,280 --> 01:29:15,030
Everything is forgotten in time.
Empires fall. So do emperors.

804
01:29:15,030 --> 01:29:16,870
Why wait?

805
01:29:16,870 --> 01:29:20,240
I will gut him right now!
No, no, no!

806
01:29:20,240 --> 01:29:23,540
Let them be. Come! Come!

807
01:29:23,540 --> 01:29:25,540
His death must be public.

808
01:29:25,540 --> 01:29:27,040
Public?

809
01:29:27,040 --> 01:29:30,160
Hang his entrails
from the city gates!

810
01:29:30,160 --> 01:29:31,580
And crucify her!

811
01:29:32,500 --> 01:29:33,880
Crucify her!

812
01:29:33,890 --> 01:29:35,810
Take them away!

813
01:29:35,800 --> 01:29:39,310
Shh! Shh! Shh!

814
01:29:52,600 --> 01:29:53,570
Thank you, Macrinus.

815
01:30:00,160 --> 01:30:01,410
Come on.

816
01:30:04,700 --> 01:30:06,700
In these last days,

817
01:30:06,700 --> 01:30:10,040
I have come to think of you
not as a subject

818
01:30:10,040 --> 01:30:12,370
but as a true friend.

819
01:30:12,370 --> 01:30:13,870
Thank you.

820
01:30:14,380 --> 01:30:16,770
Thank you so much.
But as a friend,

821
01:30:16,760 --> 01:30:19,680
I must counsel caution.

822
01:30:19,680 --> 01:30:22,600
Acacius is a hero of Rome.

823
01:30:23,550 --> 01:30:27,050
Crucifixion
is for thieves.

824
01:30:27,050 --> 01:30:28,300
Christians.

825
01:30:29,610 --> 01:30:32,110
It's too common.
                He is a traitor.
                He must die.

826
01:30:32,610 --> 01:30:33,860
I agree.

827
01:30:33,860 --> 01:30:39,870
Let the gods decide
his fate in the Colosseum.

828
01:30:46,120 --> 01:30:47,620
Let the gods decide.

829
01:30:50,490 --> 01:30:54,660
You know, last night I woke,
dreaming of a dark river.

830
01:30:56,170 --> 01:30:58,170
This time,
for the first time,

831
01:30:58,170 --> 01:30:59,670
I was crossing it.

832
01:31:00,420 --> 01:31:02,220
Hm.

833
01:31:02,220 --> 01:31:04,720
Well, you know,
where I come from,

834
01:31:04,730 --> 01:31:07,740
crossing a river,
it represents forgiveness.

835
01:31:07,730 --> 01:31:10,730
Represents... salvation.

836
01:31:10,730 --> 01:31:14,230
Where I come from,
it means
you're already dead.

837
01:31:22,530 --> 01:31:24,830
But as I saw it,
I was not afraid.

838
01:31:26,660 --> 01:31:28,160
For...

839
01:31:28,170 --> 01:31:31,290
For someone was waiting
for me on the other side.

840
01:31:32,840 --> 01:31:34,340
There.

841
01:31:45,050 --> 01:31:46,550
Who is this man?

842
01:31:47,550 --> 01:31:49,050
Scratched out?

843
01:31:50,050 --> 01:31:51,970
Maximus.

844
01:31:54,780 --> 01:31:56,650
I saw him fight once.

845
01:31:58,150 --> 01:31:59,660
He was magnificent.
Mm.

846
01:31:59,650 --> 01:32:02,650
Yeah. My time in the arena,
it was after his,

847
01:32:02,650 --> 01:32:06,950
but many still talked of him
in whispers, you know?

848
01:32:06,950 --> 01:32:09,290
Spoke of him.

849
01:32:09,790 --> 01:32:11,660
What he did.

850
01:32:11,660 --> 01:32:13,580
I met him once.

851
01:32:15,580 --> 01:32:17,080
He was kind.

852
01:32:19,580 --> 01:32:21,080
He bowed to no one.

853
01:32:24,590 --> 01:32:26,390
Come with me.

854
01:32:26,390 --> 01:32:29,230
Hmm?
Come. With me.

855
01:32:48,500 --> 01:32:52,710
When a rebel gladiator dies,
we bury them here.

856
01:32:52,700 --> 01:32:57,090
"What we do in life
echoes in eternity."

857
01:33:14,810 --> 01:33:16,730
This is Argento.

858
01:33:16,720 --> 01:33:18,440
This is Scatto.

859
01:33:58,730 --> 01:34:00,520
Cheers.

860
01:34:01,320 --> 01:34:02,600
And stop.

861
01:34:04,410 --> 01:34:08,280
For his treason
against the lives

862
01:34:08,280 --> 01:34:12,510
of the emperors
and the Roman state,

863
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:15,780
General Justus Acacius,

864
01:34:17,250 --> 01:34:20,200
an enemy of the people!

865
01:34:20,200 --> 01:34:22,960
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

866
01:34:22,960 --> 01:34:25,210
We love you, Acacius!
You are a hero!

867
01:34:26,680 --> 01:34:29,680
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

868
01:35:01,130 --> 01:35:03,830
<i>- Vae victis.
- </i>General.

869
01:35:25,850 --> 01:35:27,650
Acacius!

870
01:35:28,990 --> 01:35:33,190
Acacius! Acacius! Acacius!

871
01:35:39,330 --> 01:35:43,250
From the vanquished city
of Numidia,

872
01:35:44,590 --> 01:35:49,540
the victor of two conquests
in the Colosseum...

873
01:35:49,540 --> 01:35:52,550
Go now. <i>Vae victis.</i>

874
01:35:56,430 --> 01:35:59,350
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

875
01:35:59,350 --> 01:36:02,020
Hanno!

876
01:36:02,020 --> 01:36:04,520
Oh, Lord, any honor I have,

877
01:36:05,030 --> 01:36:06,200
I will give it to you!
                It's too late.

878
01:36:06,780 --> 01:36:09,810
The Roman traitor or

879
01:36:09,810 --> 01:36:12,310
the barbarian hero.

880
01:36:13,320 --> 01:36:14,780
Let the gods decide.

881
01:36:14,790 --> 01:36:16,630
Lucius... wait.

882
01:36:17,990 --> 01:36:19,490
Wait! Wait!

883
01:36:29,130 --> 01:36:32,130
I am a vessel.

884
01:36:33,550 --> 01:36:35,550
Fill me with vengeance

885
01:36:36,470 --> 01:36:38,810
and vanquish the betrayer.

886
01:36:56,530 --> 01:36:58,910
We love you, Acacius!
                Move it!

887
01:37:03,080 --> 01:37:04,750
Pick it up!

888
01:37:04,750 --> 01:37:07,120
Bravo, Hanno!

889
01:37:07,120 --> 01:37:08,620
We love you, Acacius!

890
01:37:08,620 --> 01:37:09,620
What are you waiting for?

891
01:37:10,120 --> 01:37:10,960
You will die!

892
01:37:41,740 --> 01:37:43,160
I know who you are.

893
01:37:45,080 --> 01:37:47,090
Lucius Verus Aurelius.

894
01:38:00,390 --> 01:38:02,420
Acacius
has raised his hand!

895
01:38:03,230 --> 01:38:05,590
He has surrendered.

896
01:38:13,070 --> 01:38:15,320
Let the gods decide.

897
01:38:33,010 --> 01:38:35,510
The gods have rendered
their judgment.

898
01:38:39,050 --> 01:38:40,560
Do what you must.

899
01:38:41,380 --> 01:38:43,680
But on my death,
you have to know...

900
01:38:45,690 --> 01:38:47,700
I love your mother,
Lucilla.

901
01:38:49,190 --> 01:38:50,690
And your father...

902
01:38:53,190 --> 01:38:54,140
Maximus.

903
01:38:55,610 --> 01:38:57,610
I would have died
for him.

904
01:38:57,610 --> 01:38:59,570
Kill him!

905
01:38:59,570 --> 01:39:02,570
Let him live!
Please!

906
01:39:03,450 --> 01:39:06,660
Live! Live! Live! Live!

907
01:39:13,500 --> 01:39:15,300
Kill him!

908
01:39:17,130 --> 01:39:18,330
Kill him!

909
01:39:18,340 --> 01:39:19,560
Archers!

910
01:39:19,550 --> 01:39:21,420
- No!
-      Kill him!

911
01:39:21,420 --> 01:39:24,170
Acacius! Acacius!

912
01:39:24,170 --> 01:39:25,890
Kill him!

913
01:39:25,890 --> 01:39:27,310
Kill him!

914
01:39:27,310 --> 01:39:29,060
Kill him! Kill him!

915
01:39:31,150 --> 01:39:32,430
Acacius!

916
01:39:42,410 --> 01:39:43,410
No!

917
01:39:44,190 --> 01:39:45,830
No!

918
01:39:45,830 --> 01:39:47,610
Acacius!

919
01:39:50,250 --> 01:39:52,030
Damn you!

920
01:39:53,870 --> 01:39:55,750
Death will be
too good for you!

921
01:40:01,350 --> 01:40:04,360
Is this how Rome
treats its heroes?

922
01:40:08,520 --> 01:40:10,050
Tell me!

923
01:40:12,360 --> 01:40:16,700
If his life has no value,
what are yours worth?

924
01:40:16,690 --> 01:40:21,860
The gods have spoken!

925
01:40:35,630 --> 01:40:39,580
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

926
01:40:54,820 --> 01:40:57,780
For our own safety,
we should return to the palace.

927
01:41:06,490 --> 01:41:09,500
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

928
01:41:19,040 --> 01:41:21,420
Stay back! Stay back!

929
01:42:09,890 --> 01:42:14,010
Arishat!

930
01:42:31,610 --> 01:42:33,110
We had a bargain.

931
01:42:37,120 --> 01:42:40,090
I gave him to you.
You let him live.

932
01:42:40,090 --> 01:42:41,950
And you got
what you wanted.

933
01:42:41,960 --> 01:42:44,680
I always get what I want.
Why did you let him live?

934
01:42:44,680 --> 01:42:47,550
You bought a gladiator,
not a slave.

935
01:42:49,550 --> 01:42:51,010
My will is my own.

936
01:42:53,470 --> 01:42:54,800
Ah...

937
01:42:54,800 --> 01:42:57,640
How blue is your blood?

938
01:42:57,640 --> 01:43:00,140
Perhaps the heart of a Roman

939
01:43:00,140 --> 01:43:02,640
beats in that chest.

940
01:43:08,150 --> 01:43:11,150
The greatest temple
Rome ever built.

941
01:43:11,150 --> 01:43:12,650
The Colosseum.

942
01:43:12,650 --> 01:43:15,150
Because this is
what they believe in.

943
01:43:15,160 --> 01:43:16,670
Power.

944
01:43:16,660 --> 01:43:19,660
They gather here to watch
the strong strike down the weak.

945
01:43:19,660 --> 01:43:21,540
There has to be
                something else.
There is nothing else.

946
01:43:21,550 --> 01:43:24,340
There has to be
                another Rome.
There is no other Rome.

947
01:43:25,800 --> 01:43:27,300
The "dream"?
                    Mm.

948
01:43:27,800 --> 01:43:29,300
The dream of Rome?

949
01:43:29,800 --> 01:43:31,140
It's an old man's fantasy.

950
01:43:33,010 --> 01:43:34,510
Who are you?

951
01:43:37,510 --> 01:43:40,400
What was your name
before you traded it
for a Roman one?

952
01:43:41,260 --> 01:43:42,760
You'll never know.

953
01:43:45,770 --> 01:43:47,270
I have a destiny.

954
01:43:50,770 --> 01:43:53,280
The gods delivered you to me.

955
01:43:56,280 --> 01:43:57,660
You will be my instrument.

956
01:43:57,660 --> 01:44:01,370
I will never be
your instrument,
in this life or the next.

957
01:44:09,430 --> 01:44:12,890
That will not be my destiny.

958
01:44:14,880 --> 01:44:16,350
But I will see your end.

959
01:44:37,370 --> 01:44:39,290
What else could I do?

960
01:44:39,290 --> 01:44:41,210
He and his bitch
were plotting to kill us.

961
01:44:41,210 --> 01:44:43,990
Don't you hear them?
They're calling for our heads!

962
01:44:43,990 --> 01:44:45,790
The Praetorians
will put down this crowd.

963
01:44:46,380 --> 01:44:48,050
Like they have every other.
You brought this on us.

964
01:44:48,050 --> 01:44:50,470
Filthy ape!

965
01:44:53,970 --> 01:44:56,720
Perhaps you should, uh,

966
01:44:57,220 --> 01:45:01,340
take Dondus elsewhere
to comfort him?

967
01:45:10,740 --> 01:45:13,110
Forgive
my brother's outburst.

968
01:45:15,030 --> 01:45:16,540
The disease
that infects his loins

969
01:45:16,530 --> 01:45:18,530
has spread to his brain.

970
01:45:18,530 --> 01:45:22,030
Every day he gets worse.
        I will reason with him.

971
01:45:38,100 --> 01:45:41,270
I see you.

972
01:45:41,270 --> 01:45:43,440
I see you.

973
01:45:44,720 --> 01:45:46,720
Caracalla, Caracalla!

974
01:45:47,220 --> 01:45:48,720
Come on, stand up.

975
01:45:48,730 --> 01:45:50,900
Get up, get up.
Not you.

976
01:45:50,890 --> 01:45:52,890
All right,
there you go.

977
01:45:54,400 --> 01:45:56,780
Now, listen to me.

978
01:45:56,780 --> 01:45:58,650
What's the matter?

979
01:45:58,650 --> 01:46:01,150
Nothing's ever mine.

980
01:46:01,150 --> 01:46:03,660
Everything is ours,
always.

981
01:46:03,660 --> 01:46:07,160
Even in the womb...
he tried...

982
01:46:07,660 --> 01:46:10,830
to cut my umbilicus

983
01:46:11,330 --> 01:46:13,080
so that I couldn't have
any more air.

984
01:46:13,080 --> 01:46:15,380
You remember that,
    do you?
Certainly.

985
01:46:15,390 --> 01:46:17,650
Come, sit.
One cannot forget.

986
01:46:18,140 --> 01:46:20,140
My conscience compels me.

987
01:46:20,140 --> 01:46:21,640
What?

988
01:46:21,640 --> 01:46:23,140
Sit.

989
01:46:23,140 --> 01:46:24,640
Your brother

990
01:46:25,100 --> 01:46:27,110
means to blame you

991
01:46:27,600 --> 01:46:30,100
in front of
the entire Senate...

992
01:46:30,100 --> 01:46:31,570
But I did not do it!

993
01:46:31,570 --> 01:46:33,070
...for what's happening
in the streets.

994
01:46:33,570 --> 01:46:35,570
The chaos!
            He's lying!

995
01:46:36,070 --> 01:46:37,570
No testimony
can be more damning

996
01:46:38,070 --> 01:46:41,360
than one brother
against another.

997
01:46:41,360 --> 01:46:44,030
That's a lie!
He always lies!

998
01:46:44,030 --> 01:46:46,420
He can be very persuasive.

999
01:46:46,920 --> 01:46:49,420
So?
What will they do to me?

1000
01:46:49,420 --> 01:46:52,420
Oh, I don't dare imagine.
But imagine this:

1001
01:46:52,420 --> 01:46:54,420
What will they do to Dondus?

1002
01:46:57,630 --> 01:47:00,130
What will they do

1003
01:47:00,630 --> 01:47:01,630
to Dondus?

1004
01:47:04,130 --> 01:47:05,470
It's your decision.

1005
01:47:43,510 --> 01:47:44,010
Brother.

1006
01:47:48,010 --> 01:47:49,510
Put down the blade.

1007
01:47:49,510 --> 01:47:51,010
You lie.

1008
01:47:51,010 --> 01:47:52,510
Give it to me.
You always lie!

1009
01:47:53,020 --> 01:47:53,830
Give it--

1010
01:47:57,770 --> 01:47:59,690
Look at me.
Look at me. Look at me.

1011
01:48:00,190 --> 01:48:02,190
Lie!
    Listen to me.
    Break the spell.

1012
01:48:02,690 --> 01:48:04,690
Lie!
    Break the spell!

1013
01:48:04,690 --> 01:48:07,610
I've always protected you.
Because I love you.

1014
01:48:08,620 --> 01:48:10,290
Come back. Help me.

1015
01:48:33,270 --> 01:48:34,270
Lucius.

1016
01:48:56,080 --> 01:48:58,580
Never could have imagined
the fates would lead us here.

1017
01:49:01,080 --> 01:49:02,580
And yet here we are.

1018
01:49:04,390 --> 01:49:06,220
Everything has
brought us full circle.

1019
01:49:06,220 --> 01:49:09,220
You sent me away
and yet fate

1020
01:49:09,230 --> 01:49:11,990
brought me back
to the very ground
where he died.

1021
01:49:14,760 --> 01:49:15,760
This ring...

1022
01:49:17,770 --> 01:49:19,770
belonged to my father.

1023
01:49:23,770 --> 01:49:26,780
He gave it
to your father,
Maximus,

1024
01:49:26,780 --> 01:49:28,780
as a token of trust.

1025
01:49:29,780 --> 01:49:33,030
I gave it to Acacius
for his valor.

1026
01:49:37,340 --> 01:49:39,840
This ring belonged to my wife.

1027
01:49:42,840 --> 01:49:44,180
I shall wear it next to yours.

1028
01:49:58,310 --> 01:50:00,810
I am truly sorry for Acacius.

1029
01:50:02,310 --> 01:50:05,060
I could not see the man.

1030
01:50:07,370 --> 01:50:08,870
He was a soldier of Rome.

1031
01:50:10,870 --> 01:50:12,370
There was a plan.

1032
01:50:13,870 --> 01:50:14,870
He was readying troops
at Ostia

1033
01:50:15,380 --> 01:50:18,390
under the command
of Darius Sextus.

1034
01:50:18,380 --> 01:50:21,380
Troops he was to lead
against the emperors.

1035
01:50:23,380 --> 01:50:27,890
Acacius. Maximus.
Marcus Aurelius.

1036
01:50:28,890 --> 01:50:31,220
They lived and died
for Rome.

1037
01:50:32,090 --> 01:50:33,590
We all do.

1038
01:50:35,600 --> 01:50:37,910
Is it true
they intend to kill you?

1039
01:50:40,680 --> 01:50:42,680
One man or another
has had a sword
against my neck

1040
01:50:43,190 --> 01:50:45,200
since the day
my father died.

1041
01:50:48,690 --> 01:50:50,690
But now
that I've found you,

1042
01:50:51,190 --> 01:50:53,190
it doesn't matter.

1043
01:50:54,700 --> 01:50:55,950
I am not afraid.

1044
01:50:55,950 --> 01:50:59,250
I've become well versed
in losing the things
that I love.

1045
01:51:02,260 --> 01:51:03,260
But now that I've found you,

1046
01:51:03,760 --> 01:51:05,260
I have no desire
to lose you again.

1047
01:51:08,760 --> 01:51:10,760
You stand like him.
Mm.

1048
01:51:11,260 --> 01:51:12,760
Alert.

1049
01:51:13,770 --> 01:51:14,680
Proud.

1050
01:51:17,140 --> 01:51:19,520
I do not have his strength.

1051
01:51:20,440 --> 01:51:22,440
I wish that were true.

1052
01:51:23,940 --> 01:51:27,230
I wish I were telling you
to flee this place.

1053
01:51:35,990 --> 01:51:36,990
Go now.

1054
01:51:45,220 --> 01:51:46,560
Strength and honor.

1055
01:51:48,890 --> 01:51:50,730
Strength and honor.

1056
01:52:03,350 --> 01:52:05,650
As Emperor,

1057
01:52:05,650 --> 01:52:07,150
I have convened

1058
01:52:08,150 --> 01:52:11,160
the Senate to appoint
my First Consul

1059
01:52:11,660 --> 01:52:14,660
and bestow upon him the power
to administer the military

1060
01:52:15,160 --> 01:52:18,160
and civic functions
of the Empire.

1061
01:52:22,170 --> 01:52:23,170
I name...

1062
01:52:24,670 --> 01:52:26,840
Citizen Dondus!

1063
01:52:33,800 --> 01:52:35,600
Hail Dondus!

1064
01:52:39,020 --> 01:52:40,440
Hail Dondus!

1065
01:52:42,360 --> 01:52:45,370
Hail Dondus.
Hail Dondus!

1066
01:52:45,360 --> 01:52:47,730
Hail Dondus!

1067
01:52:51,980 --> 01:52:53,820
As Second Consul...

1068
01:52:55,820 --> 01:52:57,320
I name...

1069
01:52:59,490 --> 01:53:00,990
Citizen...

1070
01:53:03,290 --> 01:53:04,540
Macrinus!

1071
01:53:07,000 --> 01:53:08,830
Hail Macrinus!

1072
01:53:08,830 --> 01:53:10,170
Hail Macrinus!

1073
01:53:10,670 --> 01:53:12,130
Hail Macrinus!

1074
01:53:14,050 --> 01:53:17,010
There will be
a triumphal parade
to celebrate.

1075
01:53:17,010 --> 01:53:18,510
There will be games

1076
01:53:18,980 --> 01:53:21,270
and mass executions.

1077
01:53:24,510 --> 01:53:27,020
Long live the Empire!

1078
01:53:28,520 --> 01:53:30,350
Long live the Empire!

1079
01:53:30,350 --> 01:53:32,350
Long live the Empire!

1080
01:53:38,530 --> 01:53:39,530
Sit down.

1081
01:53:43,120 --> 01:53:45,630
I happen to have...

1082
01:53:49,120 --> 01:53:53,120
with good fortune
and not a little skill...

1083
01:53:54,630 --> 01:53:58,180
the remaining emperor's ear.

1084
01:54:05,190 --> 01:54:07,190
I can speak logic to it...

1085
01:54:12,200 --> 01:54:14,570
and tame the madness
in the street. But...

1086
01:54:17,480 --> 01:54:19,480
to restore order...

1087
01:54:21,490 --> 01:54:22,990
I must have power...

1088
01:54:26,830 --> 01:54:29,170
and command

1089
01:54:29,660 --> 01:54:31,660
over the Praetorian Army.

1090
01:54:37,470 --> 01:54:39,250
Ballot...

1091
01:54:41,260 --> 01:54:42,760
or hand?

1092
01:54:44,760 --> 01:54:47,260
- Aye!
-                      Aye!

1093
01:54:50,770 --> 01:54:52,270
Your humble servant.

1094
01:54:56,490 --> 01:54:57,990
Put your hands down.

1095
01:55:00,490 --> 01:55:02,240
You can sit down.

1096
01:55:15,960 --> 01:55:17,460
<i>Rome must fall.</i>

1097
01:55:20,180 --> 01:55:22,180
I need only
give it a push.

1098
01:55:25,180 --> 01:55:27,190
And after Rome falls...

1099
01:55:28,190 --> 01:55:30,690
...what then?

1100
01:55:32,690 --> 01:55:34,690
You are
your father's child.

1101
01:55:36,650 --> 01:55:40,160
His dream of Rome
was never a dream.

1102
01:55:40,650 --> 01:55:42,650
It was a fiction.

1103
01:55:42,650 --> 01:55:44,570
"The best revenge is

1104
01:55:45,150 --> 01:55:48,910
to become unlike the one
who did the injury."

1105
01:55:48,910 --> 01:55:54,000
I have made myself
unlike your father.

1106
01:55:54,000 --> 01:55:57,580
He spoke of dreams,
I speak of truth.

1107
01:55:57,580 --> 01:55:59,920
And the only truth
in my Rome

1108
01:56:01,420 --> 01:56:03,920
is the law
of the strongest.

1109
01:56:06,180 --> 01:56:07,190
I was owned

1110
01:56:08,680 --> 01:56:10,180
by an emperor.

1111
01:56:13,480 --> 01:56:15,480
Now I control an empire.

1112
01:56:16,490 --> 01:56:20,000
Where else but in Rome
can a man do that?

1113
01:56:24,910 --> 01:56:29,610
Do you recognize
your father's mark on me?

1114
01:56:34,450 --> 01:56:35,750
If there is anything

1115
01:56:36,540 --> 01:56:38,040
you need...

1116
01:56:39,430 --> 01:56:41,300
in these last hours,

1117
01:56:42,300 --> 01:56:43,810
we will provide.

1118
01:56:49,440 --> 01:56:52,280
Your death will clear my path
to the throne.

1119
01:56:54,140 --> 01:56:57,110
Tomorrow
there will be games.

1120
01:56:57,110 --> 01:56:59,060
And at them...

1121
01:56:59,560 --> 01:57:01,560
I will prevail.

1122
01:57:15,380 --> 01:57:16,630
Ravi!

1123
01:57:23,300 --> 01:57:25,550
Can you get me a message
to Ostia by morning?

1124
01:57:25,560 --> 01:57:27,350
What is in Ostia?

1125
01:57:27,340 --> 01:57:28,840
There is an army.

1126
01:57:31,180 --> 01:57:32,680
I'm asking you
to risk yourself, my friend,

1127
01:57:32,680 --> 01:57:34,980
in the service
of something greater.

1128
01:57:37,820 --> 01:57:39,570
Ride to Ostia.

1129
01:57:40,350 --> 01:57:42,850
Take this ring
to General Darius Sextus.

1130
01:57:42,860 --> 01:57:44,370
Are you listening?

1131
01:57:44,860 --> 01:57:47,360
Darius Sextus.

1132
01:57:47,360 --> 01:57:49,610
He will know it
as Acacius's ring.

1133
01:57:52,420 --> 01:57:54,930
And, uh,

1134
01:57:55,420 --> 01:57:56,920
who shall I say has

1135
01:57:57,920 --> 01:57:59,250
sent me with this ring?

1136
01:58:02,630 --> 01:58:05,140
I am Lucius Verus Aurelius.

1137
01:58:06,130 --> 01:58:07,630
The Prince of Rome.

1138
01:58:09,130 --> 01:58:10,630
Tell him
I am summoning the army

1139
01:58:10,630 --> 01:58:13,130
to the defense
of a new Republic.

1140
01:58:21,310 --> 01:58:22,730
Should I trust you?
Yes.

1141
01:58:22,730 --> 01:58:25,150
Should I?
Yes.

1142
01:58:31,650 --> 01:58:34,410
Ravi! I need your keys.

1143
01:58:40,410 --> 01:58:42,300
Thank you.

1144
01:59:19,950 --> 01:59:22,450
Stop! Come back!

1145
01:59:53,370 --> 01:59:54,370
Who gave you this?

1146
01:59:55,370 --> 01:59:57,870
Lucius Verus Aurelius.

1147
01:59:58,870 --> 02:00:00,160
The Prince of Rome.

1148
02:00:53,380 --> 02:00:56,260
Must we kill Lucilla?

1149
02:00:58,180 --> 02:01:01,600
Until she dies,
you will never know peace.

1150
02:01:03,560 --> 02:01:04,570
Ever.

1151
02:01:15,280 --> 02:01:18,290
The people love her.
Her death will incite the mob.

1152
02:01:18,290 --> 02:01:20,790
If she dies and the streets
rise up in anger,

1153
02:01:20,790 --> 02:01:22,290
I shall deliver them
Caracalla's head

1154
02:01:22,290 --> 02:01:23,790
and the people
shall acclaim me.

1155
02:01:23,790 --> 02:01:27,800
That, my friend,
is politics.

1156
02:01:30,420 --> 02:01:32,260
Shall we?
Yes.

1157
02:01:47,520 --> 02:01:49,480
Today will be
your last fight, champion.

1158
02:01:50,490 --> 02:01:52,330
And our master
has bestowed on you...

1159
02:01:54,690 --> 02:01:57,070
the wooden sword of freedom.

1160
02:02:00,860 --> 02:02:02,860
But you have to
earn it first.

1161
02:02:03,370 --> 02:02:05,630
Today, you're gonna
defend your mother.

1162
02:02:12,090 --> 02:02:14,430
...

1163
02:02:28,440 --> 02:02:31,230
Wood or steel,
a point is still a point!

1164
02:02:58,590 --> 02:03:00,000
Wait for me.

1165
02:03:18,910 --> 02:03:20,740
In honor

1166
02:03:20,740 --> 02:03:25,110
of the acclamation
of Emperor Caracalla,

1167
02:03:25,110 --> 02:03:31,200
First Consul Dondus
and Second Consul Macrinus,

1168
02:03:31,200 --> 02:03:35,540
and as punishment
for her conspiracy
against the empire,

1169
02:03:36,040 --> 02:03:40,430
for her calumnies against
the emperor's imperial bloodline

1170
02:03:40,430 --> 02:03:42,430
and for fomenting
military mutiny

1171
02:03:42,930 --> 02:03:44,300
along with her husband,

1172
02:03:44,300 --> 02:03:48,190
the queen will face
divine justice

1173
02:03:48,190 --> 02:03:52,140
at the hands
of the Praetorian Guard.

1174
02:04:16,720 --> 02:04:18,510
I am not a general.

1175
02:04:20,000 --> 02:04:23,390
But we are all soldiers.

1176
02:04:25,310 --> 02:04:27,170
And up until now,

1177
02:04:27,180 --> 02:04:31,520
we have fought for nothing more
than another day's survival.

1178
02:04:31,510 --> 02:04:33,430
What will you
have us do?

1179
02:04:34,900 --> 02:04:35,900
Well, you can return
to your cells

1180
02:04:36,400 --> 02:04:38,240
if you do not wish
to fight this battle.

1181
02:04:38,240 --> 02:04:40,600
Or...

1182
02:04:42,610 --> 02:04:43,610
you can join me.

1183
02:04:45,110 --> 02:04:47,610
And fight for a freedom
far beyond these walls.

1184
02:04:47,610 --> 02:04:48,860
Aye!

1185
02:04:48,860 --> 02:04:53,420
There once was a time when
honor meant something in Rome.

1186
02:04:55,200 --> 02:04:56,700
In this Rome

1187
02:04:57,710 --> 02:04:59,710
I no longer believe
that exists.

1188
02:04:59,710 --> 02:05:01,710
We must find it!

1189
02:05:04,210 --> 02:05:05,710
And know this:

1190
02:05:07,220 --> 02:05:10,640
Where death is, we are not.

1191
02:05:12,550 --> 02:05:14,520
Where we are,

1192
02:05:15,520 --> 02:05:16,970
death is not!

1193
02:05:19,980 --> 02:05:21,480
By my sword.

1194
02:05:23,280 --> 02:05:25,030
Strength and honor.

1195
02:05:25,030 --> 02:05:27,200
Strength and honor!

1196
02:05:27,200 --> 02:05:28,870
Strength and honor!

1197
02:05:28,870 --> 02:05:30,740
Strength and honor!

1198
02:05:55,730 --> 02:05:57,730
Let it not be said

1199
02:05:57,730 --> 02:06:00,730
that the emperor
is not merciful.

1200
02:06:00,740 --> 02:06:06,250
The queen will be granted
a single gladiator

1201
02:06:06,740 --> 02:06:10,240
to defend her against
the Praetorian Guard.

1202
02:06:20,210 --> 02:06:24,220
The champion, Hanno!

1203
02:06:28,210 --> 02:06:31,720
Hanno! Hanno! Hanno!

1204
02:07:37,080 --> 02:07:38,950
Yes!

1205
02:07:43,090 --> 02:07:44,960
Summon the cavalry.
Put this down at once.

1206
02:07:46,380 --> 02:07:48,850
This is war! Real war!

1207
02:07:53,770 --> 02:07:57,190
The army of Acacius
is advancing
just outside of Rome, sir.

1208
02:08:00,190 --> 02:08:01,190
We can still
outflank them.

1209
02:08:01,690 --> 02:08:03,720
They have only
5,000 troops, no more.

1210
02:08:05,230 --> 02:08:06,640
How many are we?

1211
02:08:06,650 --> 02:08:08,070
Six thousand.
Perhaps more.

1212
02:08:08,060 --> 02:08:09,950
Ride to the gate
and hold them.

1213
02:09:01,780 --> 02:09:02,700
Filthy scum!

1214
02:09:16,520 --> 02:09:18,230
Lucius!

1215
02:09:19,850 --> 02:09:21,020
Give me the bow.

1216
02:09:44,710 --> 02:09:47,240
Go, my son. Lucius--

1217
02:09:47,250 --> 02:09:48,560
Shh-sh-sh-sh...

1218
02:09:48,550 --> 02:09:49,910
Horse!

1219
02:11:22,810 --> 02:11:24,930
Will nothing
kill this barbarian?

1220
02:11:24,930 --> 02:11:27,590
My name is
Lucius Verus Aurelius!

1221
02:11:27,600 --> 02:11:29,940
A man does not become
emperor by bloodline alone.

1222
02:11:29,930 --> 02:11:32,850
It must be taken by force
and kept by force.

1223
02:11:32,850 --> 02:11:34,740
Are you such a man
as this?

1224
02:11:34,740 --> 02:11:36,190
I don't fight for power.

1225
02:11:36,190 --> 02:11:39,190
I fight to free Rome
from men like you

1226
02:11:39,190 --> 02:11:40,660
and to return it to them.

1227
02:11:40,660 --> 02:11:43,610
The gods themselves
want Rome reborn.

1228
02:11:43,610 --> 02:11:46,580
They sent me...
to fulfill that task.

1229
02:11:46,580 --> 02:11:50,080
And what if your gods
sent me here to kill you?

1230
02:11:50,590 --> 02:11:51,460
Huh?

1231
02:11:52,840 --> 02:11:54,790
It's time to end this, Macrinus!

1232
02:12:30,740 --> 02:12:33,130
- Hah!
-

1233
02:13:03,160 --> 02:13:04,660
Strength and honor,

1234
02:13:05,160 --> 02:13:06,580
my son.

1235
02:14:39,870 --> 02:14:41,710
You look to me to speak.

1236
02:14:44,090 --> 02:14:45,540
I know not what
to say other than

1237
02:14:45,540 --> 02:14:48,010
we have all known
too much death.

1238
02:14:48,880 --> 02:14:52,550
Let no more blood be spilt
in the name of tyranny.

1239
02:14:56,300 --> 02:14:59,020
My grandfather,
Marcus Aurelius,

1240
02:14:59,020 --> 02:15:01,810
talked of a dream
that would be Rome.

1241
02:15:02,780 --> 02:15:04,730
A dream that my father,

1242
02:15:06,200 --> 02:15:08,980
Maximus Decimus Meridius,

1243
02:15:08,980 --> 02:15:10,780
died for.

1244
02:15:11,650 --> 02:15:13,540
An ideal.

1245
02:15:16,040 --> 02:15:20,290
A city for the many
and a refuge
for those in need.

1246
02:15:20,800 --> 02:15:23,090
A home worth fighting for.

1247
02:15:24,380 --> 02:15:28,550
A home that Maximus
spent his life defending.

1248
02:15:30,420 --> 02:15:32,310
That dream is lost.

1249
02:15:38,400 --> 02:15:39,850
But dare we...

1250
02:15:41,320 --> 02:15:44,160
rebuild that dream
together?

1251
02:15:56,000 --> 02:15:58,000
What say you?

1252
02:16:03,960 --> 02:16:05,930
Aye!

1253
02:16:07,180 --> 02:16:08,390
Aye!

1254
02:16:09,340 --> 02:16:10,340
Aye!

1255
02:16:10,350 --> 02:16:15,060
Aye! Aye! Aye! Aye!

1256
02:17:19,660 --> 02:17:20,660
Mother.

1257
02:18:13,380 --> 02:18:15,670
Speak to me, Father.
